
========================================================================
  WIGGLY vs BLUE/BLACK LINES AT n=4
========================================================================

  V_unmerged = 4, V_merged = 3, m = 6

  BLUE/BLACK LINES (complement pairing):
  Every line connects a tiling to its complement.
  In the merged graph: ALL blue/black lines are SELF-LOOPS
  (because complement pairs are merged into the same node).

  WIGGLY LINES (single-tile flips):
  Total wiggly lines: 192 (= 2^m × m / 2 = 192)
  Self-loops (same merged node): 72
  Cross-edges (different merged nodes): 120
  Distinct merged-node pairs connected: 3

  COMPARISON:
  Blue/black lines: 0 inter-node edges (all self-loops)
  Wiggly lines: 3 inter-node edges
  The meta-graph has E = 3 edges (ALL from wiggly lines)

  Blue/black lines connect TILINGS (one-to-one complement pairing)
  Wiggly lines connect TILINGS (one-to-m single-flip)
  Meta-graph edges = wiggly lines projected to merged nodes

  UNMERGED GRAPH:
  Blue/black edges (complement pairs): 1
  Wiggly edges (single-flip pairs): 5
  Both: 0
  Blue/black only: 1
  Wiggly only: 5

  NO edges are both blue/black and wiggly.
  The complement is NEVER reachable by a single arc flip.

